  "story_en": "Paul finishes crossing the bridge and walks two blocks. Ahead, the tall clock tower rises above the central station. Travelers carry heavy suitcases through the main entrance.\n\nPaul enters the busy hall and looks for the ticket window. A line of passengers waits quietly. When it is his turn, an agent behind the glass smiles.\n\n“Good morning,” the agent says. “Where can I book your ticket today?”\n\n“I need a single ticket to North Peak station,” Paul replies.\n\n“The next departure leaves at ten in the morning,” the agent explains, typing on a computer screen. “Platform four.”\n\n“Perfect,” Paul says. He pays the fare and receives his paper ticket. “Have a safe journey,” the agent adds as Paul takes his receipt.",
